I did it!

After playing for about 9 or 10 years (I can't remember if I started
in 1994 or 1995, it was the DOS Version of nethack back then) with
long pauses and varying amounts of spoilers, I finally made my first
real ascension by letting myself get _heavily_ spoiled.

(Yes... I admit it... I savescummed a healer to astral back in the
days. Let's not talk about that now.)

I started to lurk in this newsgroup again, read every spoiler I could
get hold of and started to hang out in two nethack channels on IRC
about three months ago. My thanks go to the guys in #nethack on
freenode.net.

This account is from memory, as I didn't keep any notes. I may get the
order of events mixed up a little.

I found a co-aligned altar on the second level of the dungeon and
decided to return there soon for a little service to Anhur. The first
shop in the dungeon had some interesting looking rings and 3 uncursed
scrolls of identify and with a little help from my cat I relieved
the shopkeeper of the rings and scrolls. I thought a little about
keeping the scrolls to bless them later, but decided to rather
identify the rings first. A ring of slow digestion and a +1 ring of
protection made me feel happy about that decision. (I don't remember
if I identified the =oProtection it by reading the scroll or by
letting my pet step on it and putting it on)

Fairly soon I identified a wand of create monster and decided to thank
Anhur for it by sacrificing some monsters. After the third or fourth
sacrifice, Magicbane fell on to the Altar!

With Magicbane, It was fairly safe to do sokoban and with the BoH and
a lot of more rings and wands I decided to visit the mines. I also set
up a stash in sokoban, which I kept throughout the game and very often
returned to it.

I proceeded to train my large cat named Felix to steal all the money
from every shopkeeper in the dungeon (especially minetown) and donated
it to the (cross-aligned) priest in minetown. When I finished the
mines, my trusty cat had stepped onto a polymorph trap and turned into
a golden naga and later I met a large dog called Spot which shortly
afterwards also stepped into a polymorph trap and turned into a
Jabberwock.

Now I had to keep my pets from attacking Izchak and the minetown
priest.

The minetown priest thanked me for my consideration by reducing my AC
to 0.

(But later I whistled my pets in on him. He was an infidel after all.
He deserved to die. And I needed his cloak. But Izchak remained alive
(but penniless) in his shop. :-)

Since I had found a spellbook of magic mapping somewhere, I practised
divination spells by lighting the mines up while going down.

This gave me the ability to map every level between the oracle and
medusa, sadly there was no Fort Ludios in the game. No big room
either.

Somewhere in between the mines and medusa I must have sacrificed a
little more (I remember going back to the co-aligned altar every time
I found some scrolls or wands of create monster), and got crowned
around XP level 13. Blessed +FoD, Yum!

While going down the main dungeon I suddenly saw a non-tame Jabberwock
approaching me (around dlv 10, one level below the entrance to
Sokoban). I carefully dispatched it by escaping upstairs now and then
to heal up and rehgain power. When I got to explore that level, I
found the polymorph trap that had generated it.

When I received the telepathic message from Neferet the Green, I was
still level 13, so I went down to medusa's island with my Pet
Jabberwock and Golden Naga.

On dungeon level 18 there was a sink with a hole next to it.
On dungeon level 19 I found a co-aligned altar.

That made me think: "Is it possible to lure a black pudding into a
hole?"

I proceeded to meet medusa, while thinking that I'd do some pudding
farming later.

When entering medusa's level, I had my first "interesting time" in the
game. There was a magic trap and a titan in the first room. Some
monster kept stepping onto the magic trap, and the titan kept
summoning monsters. Within 2 moves me and my pets were surrounded by
fairly buff monsters. Said titan, two black dragons (one of them
disintegrated my small shield and I made it taste my finger of
death!), a green and a red dragon, a mind flayer, a disenchanter and
whatnot. I quickly engraved Elbereth with my wand of fire. My poor
pets both died while I was watching from the stairs. I took all the
monsters out with spells and then took the risk of trying out a maybe
spoiled black dragon corpse (not really dangerous with a blessed
unicorn horn). Made me feel very firm. Taking out the fish was easy
with magic missiles and my ring of levitation made me reach medusa
safely.

For medusa I had brought a mirror as special gift, since I had had a
bad experience with letting her escape downstairs in a previous game.

(My poor Valkyrie hadn't noticed that medusa was not dead ("Hm, no
corpse?" -- No "you kill medusa!" either, dummy!) and went downstairs,
only to look her in the eye.)

Then I returned upstairs to do the quest and some pudding farming
(can't remember in which order... I think I put up my farm first.).

Luring a black pudding down the hole had worked quite well, and I had
a blooming pudding farm in no time. Anhur rewarded me with lots of
spellbooks and golden glows (but no protection), until I got bored and
decided to press on. Armor class got better, around -20 or so, but I
still hadn't found any silver or gray dragon scales (and was
unsuccesful at getting wishes from thrones and blessed magic lamps), I
decided to put on some red dragon scales (instead of studded leather
armor) and go down to the castle to get the wand of wishing and some
silver dragon scales (preferably both). I didn't enchant the red
dragon scales, because I had found very few scrolls of enchant armor
so far and I wanted to enchant only the armor I wanted to keep.

The quest was rather eventless. The dark one to escaped upstairs,
which gave me my first experience in dealing with covetous monsters.

I found a bones file from a former samurai of mine further down. By
that time I was able to cast identify and remove curse quite well, so
I got a lot of money and a whole lot of useful items from that pile.

Another temple with a cross-aligned priest was on the way to the
castle, below medusa. I decided to give him 65000 zm in chunks of
5600, but no luck. Naked AC 0 it was and stayed.

So the castle it was. I had a lot of rather fearsome spells by now, so
I wasn't afraid to clean it out.

Then I made my first (and only) fatal (!) mistake in the game.

I played the tune my god gave me and decided to stand on the
drawbridge while fighting the monsters in the interior with spells and
magicbane (by now enchanted to +2).

A captain laughed about my stupidity and zapped the drawbridge with
his wand of striking...

A huge chunk of metal hits you in the head...
But wait...

There went my "AoLS and the first attempt on my life...

I shrugged, put on my Amulet of Water Breathing, froze the moat and
continued to exact Anhurs revenge on the castle dwellers.

After the castle, which finally gave me the silver dragon scales I had
hoped for, I payed a very short visit to the VoTD, but used the
Eye to return to my stash in sokoban for some polypiling and also a
little more pudding farming (to hopefully get some protection).

Pudding farming boosted my naked armor class down to -7, which went
fairly quick, since Anhur didn't have any more unknown spellbooks to
give (I didn't get cone of cold or any cold related spells... probably
the divine bookstore was out of stock).

Polypiling yielded more useful Amulets (two more "AoLS... I decided to
be always wearing one of those in the rest of the game... "Don't take
any chances!", became my motto.), Helm of Brillance and scrolls of
Enchant Armor (I had only one scroll of charging, which I decided to
use on the wand of wishing instead of the two dried out magic markers
I found in the samurai's bones file).

After I got bored from all this pudding farming and polypiling, I
decided to use a few wishes. First wish were "blessed rustproof +2
speed boots", then I blessed the ?oCharging and used two more wishes
for gauntlets of dexterity and ... (Tadaa!) a saddle. (I simply like
riding dragons.)

All this inventory-tuning (and a little alchemy) gave me the AC, HP
and Pw you see in the screenshot.

Then I felt more than safe to enter gehennom and get the invocation
artifacts.

I mapped every level with magic mapping, casted detect monster
(skilled) a lot and detect treasure. I immediately dug my exit route
while going down.

Bribed asmodeus, and was a little puzzled by Juiblex. FoD missed him
and /oFire did nothing... then he escaped upstairs and I had to
practise my strategy for dispatching covetous monsters again (on
non-teleport levels, stand near, not next-to, the upstairs and jump in
the right moment). Magicbane killed him off, after I had to use my
unihorn a couple of times.

Baalzebub wanted a fight, as did several master and arch-lichs. Still,
Magicbane and the Eye protected me from them well enough that I didn't
consider genociding them, although I had some blessed scrolls of
genocide in my pack (for emergency-exitus).

Vlad was a real nuisance. I decided to whack him with magicbane
instead of casting magic missiles at him (which had worked well on
other vampire lords)... He got confused and decided to read a scroll
of teleportation in his deluded state... Ouch! So I have to go looking
for him now?

I decided to look for the Vibrating Square first. Found it on level 51
and then searched for Vlad on every level. I saw a grey 'V' on the
rogue level. Smart move, Vlad, but not smart enough for me! This time
he got toasted by magic missile, wall + reflection and I grabbed the
candelabrum.

After clearing out Rodney's zoo I got a little nervous. Do I have the
right inventory? I asked many questions on #nethack on freenode.net
(thanks guys!) and finally made another mistake... I decided to
freshen up all my spells. Yes, all of them, just for good measure...

Then I realised I had no way of confusing myself, since I had
diluted/cancelled all potions of booze or confusion.

So I had to hunt gehennom for potions and polypiled a little to get 4
potions of confusion (along with 4 the neede scrolls of gold
detection).

I also did a little more alchemy to get !oFH to deal with the
aftermath from Pestilence and Death.

Rodney got toasted by my Finger of Death. Then I teleported from
stairway to stairway down to the VS (with intrinsic teleportation). (I
always took lots of food with me, mostly to deal with the food
consumption required by intrinsic teleportation.)

Then my heart pounded like that of a teenager approaching his beloved
when I was standing on the vibrating square. I put on "Carlo Gesualdo
- Tenebrae, The Hilliard Ensemble" and ascended to the Astral Plane to
the sound of the responsoria from the 16th century. Moloch's sanctum
gave me a an idea of what I would have to deal with on the Astral
Plane. Mostly I was surrounded by monsters, but I dealt with Moloch's
high priest from the doorway. In Moloch's high temple I had to repair
my armor which was smouldered from all the fire traps (I had brough
enough ?oEA with me and locked the door with wizard lock).

Sadly I had to leave a bag of holding with about 7 artifacts in my
stash (Among them Excalibur, Mjollnir and the Tsurugi (from the
samurai bones), because it was too heavy.

Due to the confused gold detection trick, all elemental planes were
quite easy except from the plane of air. Air Elementals engulfed me
several times, every time I dropped the Amulet and dug myself out with
a FoD.

Luckily there were enough vortices in the plane of Air to let me
regenerate myself.

Astral gave me problems. Famine and Pestilence were easily
dispatchable by FoD or /oDeath. However all those angels and priests
and adventurers and other monsters surrounding my in front of the
temple doors gave me a hard time. Too much casting FoD (sometimes
without dropping the amulet first) which didn't work on the priests
and angels anyways made my Pw go down to 0 and my HP down to 200. So I
got a little nervous. Then I discovered that I could hide out in the
narrow corridor above the right temple (which was lawful).

Then I tamed the two dragons that attacked me from both sides and
could get a little rest. A samurai attacked me who was wearing a
Helmet of Opposite Alignment, but I decided to look for the chaotic
altar, because I didn't feel like becoming lawful after my god had
provided so well for me.

The second altar (the middle one) was neutral, but by that time I had
picked up a cockatrice corpse and I was starting to have fun on the
Astral plane. I made lots of beautiful priest and angel statues (and a
stone golem... Oh well...).

The third altar (the chaotic one) was guarded by Death, so I got a
little nervous about having to face him.

There was no reason for that. Magic missile is the wizard's friend. He
got up fairly quickly and tried to get me while I was already standing
on the altar with the amulet. I decided to kill him again for good
measure (instead of sacrificing the amulet directly). His corpse lies
to the upper right of my '@' in the screenshot.

I'm satisfied. I had intended to ascend a wizard and although the last
two promising chars were a valkyrie and a samurai, a wizard finally
made it through.

I think I spent too much timing running for my stash and I always took
a lot more items (especially wands and potions) with me than I really
needed.

Id'ing those rings early in the game and getting Magicbane before
tackling the mines were the key to the survival of this wizard. Still
he had to engrave Elbereth a lot, but a confused, stun or cancelled
monster is a lot less of an issue even for an inexperienced char.

I think I'll try to ascend a valk, samurai or a barbarian on the next
attempt. And I think I'll genocide 'L', because I've heard they are a
lot more trouble if you're not wielding Magicbane. I didn't really
care about any conduct, but I also didn't feel the need to polymorph
myself or genocide any monster, so I didn't.

